1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,977
A dbt project is code: SQL and YAML files.

2
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:13,119
Git keeps the history of that code, so you can see what changed, undo a mistake, and work with others.

3
00:00:14,069 --> 00:00:15,757
GitHub keeps a copy online.

4
00:00:16,037 --> 00:00:19,674
Others can see your work there, and later it runs your pipeline for you.

5
00:00:20,624 --> 00:00:21,553
Here is the loop.

6
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:23,958
You change files in your project folder.

7
00:00:24,908 --> 00:00:29,277
You commit them: a snapshot with a short message, made in Studio's Git tab.

8
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:31,807
You push the commits to GitHub.

9
00:00:32,087 --> 00:00:35,421
In Studio, that is Publish Branch the first time, then Push.

10
00:00:36,371 --> 00:00:44,779
And from lesson 2.2 on, each lesson's work goes on its own branch, and becomes a pull request on GitHub, which we merge into main.

11
00:00:45,729 --> 00:00:47,423
Let's create the repository.

12
00:00:47,703 --> 00:00:52,500
On GitHub, signed in, click the plus button at the top, and choose New repository.

13
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:54,229
Give it a name.

14
00:00:54,509 --> 00:00:59,913
This is a rehearsal copy, nyc taxi dbt rehearsal, and it is private.

15
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:04,992
In your own project, call it nyc taxi dbt, and make it public.

16
00:01:05,942 --> 00:01:10,129
Leave everything else empty: no README, no gitignore, no license.

17
00:01:10,409 --> 00:01:13,858
Our first commit, in lesson 2.1, brings those files.

18
00:01:14,138 --> 00:01:15,667
Click Create repository.

19
00:01:16,617 --> 00:01:18,738
The repository is ready, and empty.

20
00:01:19,018 --> 00:01:20,443
GitHub shows its address.

21
00:01:20,723 --> 00:01:25,543
Copy the HTTPS address: Studio needs it in lesson 2.1.

22
00:01:26,493 --> 00:01:27,345
One more thing.

23
00:01:27,625 --> 00:01:30,951
GitHub does not accept your account password for pushing code.

24
00:01:31,231 --> 00:01:35,082
Pushes use a personal access token: a key you create on GitHub.

25
00:01:36,032 --> 00:01:41,366
Make it work for this repository only, with contents and workflows set to read and write.

26
00:01:41,646 --> 00:01:45,111
We set it up right before the first push, in lesson 2.1.

27
00:01:46,061 --> 00:01:46,794
To recap.

28
00:01:47,074 --> 00:01:54,377
Git keeps the history, GitHub keeps a copy online, and one pull request per lesson keeps every change easy to follow.

29
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:57,069
Next, we create the dbt project.
